# Errors: SAVE writes to a sector that isn't on the disc (sector 4 of cylinder 33 side 0 removed from the copy).
# The IDC takes three records of it, then answers 10 to the fourth, which sends the sector to the disc.
# CP/M reports "Bad Sector"; Return carries on, then DIR.
drive A 480Z_RML_system-cpm2.2f-basic5.3g-basic6.3b.imd
drop A 33 0 4
seconds 70
type 2.0 B
type 12 SAVE 2 S.COM\r
type 32 \r
type 50 DIR\r
